<title>INDIA: RTRS-Cricket: Australia v India test scoreboard.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Cricket: Australia v India test scoreboard.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scoreboard on the fourth day of the one-off test match between India and Australia on Sunday.</p>
<p>Australia 182 (first innings)</p>
<p>India 361 (first innings)</p>
<p>Australia (second innings)  M.Taylor c Rathore b Kapoor	  37</p>
<p> M.Slater c Azharuddin b Johnson     0</p>
<p> R.Ponting b Prasad		     13</p>
<p> M.Waugh c Mongia b Kumble	    23</p>
<p> S.Waugh not out			  67</p>
<p> M.Bevan c Azharuddin b Kumble	33</p>
<p> I.Healy st Mongia b Kumble	   12</p>
<p> B.Hogg c Rathore b Kumble	     4</p>
<p> P.Reiffel lbw b Kumble		  6</p>
<p> P.McIntyre lbw b Prasad		16</p>
<p> G.McGrath c Mongia b Prasad	   0</p>
<p> Extras (b-9 lb-6 nb-7 w-1)	  23</p>
<p>Total (all out in 108.3  overs)  234</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-4 2-25 3-72 4-78 5-145 6-159 7-171 8-191 9-232</p>
<p>Bowling: Prasad 13.3-7-18-3, Johnson 12-2-40-1 (w-1), Kumble 41-12-67-5 (nb-6), Joshi 20-7-52-0, Kapoor 22-5-42-1 (nb-1).</p>
<p>India second innings</p>
<p> V.Rathore b Reiffel			   14</p>
<p> N.Mongia lbw b Reiffel			 0</p>
<p> S.Ganguly not out			     21</p>
<p> S.Tendulkar b McGrath			  0</p>
<p> M.Azharuddin not out			  21</p>
<p> Extras (w-1, nb-1)			     2</p>
<p>Total (for three wickets in 13.2 overs) 58</p>
<p>Did not bat: R.Dravid, S.Joshi, A.Kapoor, A.Kumble, D.Johnson, V.Prasad</p>
<p>Fall of wickets 1-1, 2-25, 3-26</p>
<p>Bowling: McGrath 7-2-30-1, Reiffel 6-2-24-2 (nb-1, w-1), McIntyre 0.2-0-4-0.</p>
<p>Result: India won by seven wickets.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
